Expected output: A page with the title "This is a test" in large bold font.

Actual output: A blank page.

Why?

The reason for the blank page is that the `center` environment is not a LaTeX environment, but rather a command that centers the contents of a document. In this case, there is no content inside the `center` environment, so there is nothing to center.

To fix this, you can add some content inside the `center` environment, like this:

\documentclass{article}
\begin{document}
\begin{center}
\LARGE
\textbf{This is a test}
\end{center}
\end{document}

This will produce the expected output, a page with the title "This is a test" in large bold font.

